From 9653dc92b6d164502b403f518ec2b369e4ee3c2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Sam (local build)" <sam@local>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:59:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] dde-emu v1e: PT-CAN DDE/EGS frame emulation on the V2
 board (opt-in TX)

- ptcan_emu_core.c (host-testable): 19 frames (0x3F9 3FD 39A 396 518 A5 D9 DC F3
  8F 2C4 281 1B9 381 3B3 397 3FB 512 592) with captured run 4 content/periods,
  E2E (CRC8 0x1D, alive counter) for 3F9/3FD/A5/D9/DC/F3/8F, KL15 from 0x12F,
  NM 0x512/0x518 release like the real ECUs, 60 s NM ceiling, 0x592 MIL-off only
- gating: TX only with PT-CAN traffic in the last 200 ms, new wake after >= 1 s
  silence, cyclics stop when KL15 off + NM released + no foreign NM for 1.95 s
- never-send list enforced in the core and again before queueing (0x137, EWS
  0x80/0x85/0x351/0x380/0x580/0x5C0, 0x6xx, 0x27A, 0x598)
- FOREIGN fault latch if one of our enabled IDs is received from another node
- ptcan_emu.c glue: controller boots Listen Only; Normal CAN 2.0 only while the
  host has TX enabled (0xa5, 20 s keepalive); bus-off / error passive / foreign /
  mode error -> Listen Only, latched until mask 0. Stats via 0xa6, console line.
- MCP251863 driver: TX FIFO2 depth (16 for EMU_CAN_TX), mcp251863_set_normal()
- CMake EMU_CAN_TX (default ON, V2 DDE emulator builds only); other V2 builds
  stay MCP251863_RX_ONLY. V1 builds have no CAN at all.
- tests: unit, E2E vectors (run 4, 0 mismatches over 30365 real frames),
  replays vs run 4 ddecan/noddecan and run 5 noegs
